For $n,k\ge1$, let $E_{n,k}=\{x:P^n(x,\cdot)\ge k^{-1}
u(\cdot)\}$. Fix a countable generating sequence $(G_j)$. The union of the finite Boolean algebras generated by $G_1,\ldots,G_j$ is a countable algebra $\mathcal A_0$ generating $\mathcal X$. The inequality defining $E_{n,k}$ is equivalent to its restrictions to $B\in\mathcal A_0$: if those hold, approximate any measurable $A$ under the finite measure $P^n(x,\cdot)+k^{-1}
u$ by an algebra set; the difference of the two sides changes by at most that symmetric-difference mass, which tends to zero. Thus $E_{n,k}= igcap_{B\in\mathcal A_0}\{x:P^n(x,B)\ge k^{-1}
u(B)\}$ is measurable by [F2] and [F4]. The statewise hypothesis makes their union the whole space. Since $
u$ is a probability, one such set has positive $
u$-mass. Integrating its inequality gives $
u P^n\ge k^{-1}
u(E_{n,k})
u$. Thus the set $T=\{n\ge1:
u P^n\ge c_n
u	ext{ for some }c_n>0\}$ is nonempty.
